<title>UK: EBRD sets 150 bln lire structured 10-year bond.</title>
<headline>EBRD sets 150 bln lire structured 10-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Banca di Roma and Morgan Stanley.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN BANK FOR RECONSTRUCTION AND DEVELOPMENT</p>
<p> AMT    150 BLN LIRE  COUPON     *10.0     MATURITY  **27.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE   FIX/REV FRN   ISS PRICE  101.625   PAY DATE    27.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.0	 REOFFER    100.0</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (M) 5-50	SALE LIMITS US/UK/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    =	   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.375     SELL CONC  1.625     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	*FOR FIRST THREE YEARS THEN 9.50 LESS TWO TIMES</p>
<p>		 SIX-MONTH LIBOR</p>
<p>	     **CALL AT PAR 27.MAR.00</p>
<p>		 ISSUED OFF THE MTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
